# Backend (Laravel)

Stack: PHP 8.2+, PSR-12, declare(strict_types=1);

Layers: Controller → FormRequest → Service → Model; out=Resource; auth=Policy

## Must
- One class = one job (SRP). SOLID where it pays off.
- Controller: get request → call Service → return Resource/response. No business logic. No validation arrays.
- FormRequest: all validation. Rules from config() for limits/defaults.
- Service: business ops, multi-model, side effects, external calls.
- Resource: only API shape. Never return Eloquent models raw.
- Policy: authorization (MVP may allow-all). Permissions later.
- Model: $fillable, $casts (+ Enum), relations, scopes. No fat logic.
- Enum: statuses/kinds/roles — never magic strings.
- config/*: limits, defaults, integrations, env-tunable values.
- API methods: OpenAPI attrs above action; request≈FormRequest, response≈Resource.
- Names: clear. DRY. No unused use.

## Never
- dd/dump/var_dump/ray, commented-out junk, dead code
- Business logic in Controller/Model
- Duplicate validation or response shaping outside FormRequest/Resource
